{"name":"Go Go Pink","hex":"#fdd8d4","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pink","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A color reminiscent of pinks, the flowers.","Magenta, the colour evoked by red and blue light when combined."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a colour between red and white; pale red.","Of a fox-hunter's jacket: scarlet."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pink"}],"entries":[{"title":"Pink","blocks":[{"text":"Pink is a pale tint of red or rose, the color of the pink flower. It was first used as a color name in the late 17th century. A combination of pink and white is associated with innocence, whereas a combination of pink and black links to eroticism and seduction."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg/330px-Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pink","wikidata":"Q429220"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/Burano_Hausfassade_W%C3%A4sche-20090315-RM-113043.jpg/500px-Burano_Hausfassade_W%C3%A4sche-20090315-RM-113043.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/Burano_Hausfassade_W%C3%A4sche-20090315-RM-113043.jpg/500px-Burano_Hausfassade_W%C3%A4sche-20090315-RM-113043.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABurano_Hausfassade_W%C3%A4sche-20090315-RM-113043.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Cherry_Blossom_Spring_Sky_%284531848988%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Cherry_Blossom_Spring_Sky_%284531848988%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Cherry_Blossom_Spring_Sky_%28453184898